1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,973
Sweetheart, on Christmas Eve of nineteen eighty-three,

2
00:00:03,973 --> 00:00:06,621
a girl of about seventeen knocked on

3
00:00:06,621 --> 00:00:08,240
my door in a blizzard,

4
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:09,785
nine months pregnant,

5
00:00:09,785 --> 00:00:11,919
with no coat and blood on her

6
00:00:11,919 --> 00:00:12,213
lip.

7
00:00:12,393 --> 00:00:13,946
She said, please,

8
00:00:13,946 --> 00:00:16,503
ma'am, can I use your phone?

9
00:00:16,683 --> 00:00:18,425
Somebody's after me.

10
00:00:18,605 --> 00:00:21,112
Every sensible person I knew told me

11
00:00:21,112 --> 00:00:23,759
afterward that I should have shut that

12
00:00:23,759 --> 00:00:24,108
door.

13
00:00:24,288 --> 00:00:25,275
I didn't.

14
00:00:25,455 --> 00:00:27,405
And that baby was born on my

15
00:00:27,405 --> 00:00:29,565
living room floor at two in the

16
00:00:29,565 --> 00:00:30,122
morning.

17
00:00:30,472 --> 00:00:32,808
Tonight I'm going to tell you who

18
00:00:32,808 --> 00:00:33,799
was after her,

19
00:00:33,799 --> 00:00:35,568
what happened that night,

20
00:00:35,568 --> 00:00:38,188
and who rang my doorbell twenty years

21
00:00:38,188 --> 00:00:40,949
later, on Christmas Eve of two thousand

22
00:00:40,949 --> 00:00:41,373
three.

23
00:00:41,553 --> 00:00:42,587
Stay with me,

24
00:00:42,587 --> 00:00:45,767
honey, because I've only told this story

25
00:00:45,767 --> 00:00:47,277
a handful of times.

26
00:00:47,457 --> 00:00:49,744
It still makes my hands shake.

27
00:00:49,924 --> 00:00:52,259
And the ending is the most beautiful

28
00:00:52,259 --> 00:00:54,789
thing that's ever happened in my house.

29
00:00:55,139 --> 00:00:56,740
That Christmas Eve,

30
00:00:56,740 --> 00:00:59,944
Harold was stuck at his brother's farm

31
00:00:59,944 --> 00:01:02,388
in Shelby, twenty miles away,

32
00:01:02,388 --> 00:01:04,833
because the roads had closed.

33
00:01:05,013 --> 00:01:07,527
Susan was away at nursing school,

34
00:01:07,527 --> 00:01:09,585
and Mark was snowed in at a

35
00:01:09,585 --> 00:01:11,642
friend's house across town.

36
00:01:11,822 --> 00:01:13,170
So it was just me,

37
00:01:13,170 --> 00:01:15,717
alone in the house on Maple Drive,

38
00:01:15,717 --> 00:01:17,740
with the radio on and a pot

39
00:01:17,740 --> 00:01:19,388
of chili on the stove,

40
00:01:19,388 --> 00:01:22,159
watching the snow pile up against the

41
00:01:22,159 --> 00:01:22,759
windows.

42
00:01:22,939 --> 00:01:25,597
The worst blizzard in ten years.

43
00:01:25,947 --> 00:01:27,188
At ten o'clock,

44
00:01:27,188 --> 00:01:29,999
somebody pounded on the back door.

45
00:01:30,179 --> 00:01:31,445
Not the front,

46
00:01:31,445 --> 00:01:34,429
the back, which nobody ever used.

47
00:01:34,609 --> 00:01:36,655
I turned on the porch light,

48
00:01:36,655 --> 00:01:38,191
and there was a girl,

49
00:01:38,191 --> 00:01:40,384
honey, a skinny girl in a thin

50
00:01:40,384 --> 00:01:42,869
sweater, with snow in her hair and

51
00:01:42,869 --> 00:01:44,843
her belly so big she had to

52
00:01:44,843 --> 00:01:46,451
hold onto the railing.

53
00:01:46,631 --> 00:01:47,885
Her lip was split,

54
00:01:47,885 --> 00:01:50,253
and she kept looking back over her

55
00:01:50,253 --> 00:01:51,855
shoulder into the dark.

56
00:01:52,205 --> 00:01:53,753
She said, please,

57
00:01:53,753 --> 00:01:55,665
can I use your phone?

58
00:01:55,845 --> 00:01:57,900
I need to call somebody.

59
00:01:58,080 --> 00:01:59,752
He's looking for me.

60
00:01:59,932 --> 00:02:01,104
And I asked,

61
00:02:01,104 --> 00:02:03,253
who's looking for you?

62
00:02:03,433 --> 00:02:04,791
And she said,

63
00:02:04,791 --> 00:02:06,149
my boyfriend.

64
00:02:06,329 --> 00:02:08,265
He's in the car on the next

65
00:02:08,265 --> 00:02:08,767
street.

66
00:02:08,947 --> 00:02:10,538
He's been drinking.

67
00:02:10,718 --> 00:02:11,844
I ran.

68
00:02:12,024 --> 00:02:14,222
In a minute I'll tell you what

69
00:02:14,222 --> 00:02:16,420
that man did when he found out

70
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:17,446
where she was.

71
00:02:17,796 --> 00:02:19,762
I'll be honest with you,

72
00:02:19,762 --> 00:02:20,663
sweetheart.

73
00:02:20,843 --> 00:02:22,168
For one second,

74
00:02:22,168 --> 00:02:23,316
I was scared.

75
00:02:23,496 --> 00:02:25,203
I was a woman alone.

76
00:02:25,383 --> 00:02:27,278
And there was a drunk man in

77
00:02:27,278 --> 00:02:29,444
a car somewhere out there in the

78
00:02:29,444 --> 00:02:29,783
snow.

79
00:02:29,963 --> 00:02:31,790
But I looked at that girl,

80
00:02:31,790 --> 00:02:33,195
shaking on my porch,

81
00:02:33,195 --> 00:02:35,584
holding her belly with both hands,

82
00:02:35,584 --> 00:02:38,113
and I thought about my own daughter.

83
00:02:38,293 --> 00:02:39,583
And I said,

84
00:02:39,583 --> 00:02:40,991
get in here,

85
00:02:40,991 --> 00:02:41,695
honey.

86
00:02:41,875 --> 00:02:42,746
Now.

87
00:02:42,926 --> 00:02:44,813
And I locked the door behind her

88
00:02:44,813 --> 00:02:46,641
and turned off the porch light.

89
00:02:46,991 --> 00:02:48,511
Her name was Angela.

90
00:02:48,691 --> 00:02:50,073
She was seventeen.

91
00:02:50,253 --> 00:02:52,924
She'd run away from home in Kentucky

92
00:02:52,924 --> 00:02:55,002
with this man a year before,

93
00:02:55,002 --> 00:02:57,377
and he'd brought her up to Ohio,

94
00:02:57,377 --> 00:02:59,158
and things had gone bad.

95
00:02:59,338 --> 00:03:00,569
Very bad.

96
00:03:00,749 --> 00:03:02,961
That night, he'd hit her in the

97
00:03:02,961 --> 00:03:05,103
car, and she'd jumped out at a

98
00:03:05,103 --> 00:03:07,886
stop sign and run through the backyards

99
00:03:07,886 --> 00:03:09,885
in the snow until she saw my

100
00:03:09,885 --> 00:03:10,884
kitchen light.

101
00:03:11,064 --> 00:03:13,189
Mine was the only one on.

102
00:03:13,539 --> 00:03:16,171
I wrapped her in Harold's big flannel

103
00:03:16,171 --> 00:03:18,093
robe, put her by the stove,

104
00:03:18,093 --> 00:03:20,156
and gave her a bowl of chili.

105
00:03:20,336 --> 00:03:22,438
And then I called the sheriff.

106
00:03:22,618 --> 00:03:24,042
The deputy said,

107
00:03:24,042 --> 00:03:27,068
ma'am, every road in the county is

108
00:03:27,068 --> 00:03:27,691
closed.

109
00:03:27,871 --> 00:03:30,576
We'll get someone there when we can.

110
00:03:30,756 --> 00:03:32,231
Keep your doors locked.

111
00:03:32,411 --> 00:03:34,729
And that's when we heard the car,

112
00:03:34,729 --> 00:03:35,151
honey.

113
00:03:35,331 --> 00:03:37,743
Driving slowly down Maple Drive,

114
00:03:37,743 --> 00:03:41,287
with its headlights sweeping across the houses.

115
00:03:41,637 --> 00:03:44,381
If you're enjoying Grandma's story,

116
00:03:44,381 --> 00:03:46,498
tap the like button for me,

117
00:03:46,498 --> 00:03:47,360
sweetheart.

118
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:50,733
It helps more people find these stories.

119
00:03:50,913 --> 00:03:53,109
The car stopped in front of my

120
00:03:53,109 --> 00:03:53,548
house.

121
00:03:53,728 --> 00:03:56,427
A man got out and started walking

122
00:03:56,427 --> 00:03:57,899
up my front steps,

123
00:03:57,899 --> 00:03:59,290
yelling her name.

124
00:03:59,470 --> 00:04:00,456
Angela!

125
00:04:00,636 --> 00:04:03,144
Angela, I know you're in there!

126
00:04:03,324 --> 00:04:05,464
And he pounded on the front door

127
00:04:05,464 --> 00:04:07,538
so hard the pictures on my wall

128
00:04:07,538 --> 00:04:08,073
rattled.

129
00:04:08,253 --> 00:04:11,097
Angela crawled under my kitchen table.

130
00:04:11,448 --> 00:04:12,824
I want you to know,

131
00:04:12,824 --> 00:04:14,489
honey, I was terrified.

132
00:04:14,669 --> 00:04:16,589
But I went to that door,

133
00:04:16,589 --> 00:04:18,268
and I didn't open it.

134
00:04:18,448 --> 00:04:20,117
I said through the door,

135
00:04:20,117 --> 00:04:22,202
as loud and steady as I could,

136
00:04:22,202 --> 00:04:24,010
the sheriff is on his way.

137
00:04:24,190 --> 00:04:26,117
There's nobody here for you.

138
00:04:26,297 --> 00:04:28,262
And then I said the thing my

139
00:04:28,262 --> 00:04:30,437
mother always told me to say to

140
00:04:30,437 --> 00:04:30,999
a bully.

141
00:04:31,179 --> 00:04:32,487
I said, go home,

142
00:04:32,487 --> 00:04:35,594
young man, before you do something you

143
00:04:35,594 --> 00:04:36,903
can't take back.

144
00:04:37,253 --> 00:04:39,729
Then I did something I'd never done

145
00:04:39,729 --> 00:04:40,225
before.

146
00:04:40,405 --> 00:04:43,046
I went and got Harold's deer rifle

147
00:04:43,046 --> 00:04:44,445
out of the closet.

148
00:04:44,625 --> 00:04:46,227
It wasn't loaded.

149
00:04:46,407 --> 00:04:48,830
I didn't even know where he kept

150
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:49,739
the bullets.

151
00:04:49,919 --> 00:04:51,919
But I stood in my front window

152
00:04:51,919 --> 00:04:52,985
with that rifle,

153
00:04:52,985 --> 00:04:55,185
where he could see me through the

154
00:04:55,185 --> 00:04:55,585
glass.

155
00:04:55,765 --> 00:04:57,732
He looked at me for a long

156
00:04:57,732 --> 00:04:58,261
minute.

157
00:04:58,441 --> 00:05:00,772
Then he got back in his car

158
00:05:00,772 --> 00:05:03,189
and drove off into the snow.

159
00:05:03,369 --> 00:05:05,663
And I sat down on the floor,

160
00:05:05,663 --> 00:05:07,712
because my legs gave out.

161
00:05:08,061 --> 00:05:10,831
Angela came out from under the table,

162
00:05:10,831 --> 00:05:12,103
white as a sheet,

163
00:05:12,103 --> 00:05:14,498
and we sat together by the stove

164
00:05:14,498 --> 00:05:15,545
for two hours,

165
00:05:15,545 --> 00:05:17,791
honey, listening to every car.

166
00:05:17,971 --> 00:05:20,239
She told me about her mother back

167
00:05:20,239 --> 00:05:22,852
in Kentucky, whom she hadn't called in

168
00:05:22,852 --> 00:05:24,983
a year because she was ashamed.

169
00:05:25,163 --> 00:05:26,716
I said, sweetheart,

170
00:05:26,716 --> 00:05:29,412
your mother isn't ashamed of you.

171
00:05:29,592 --> 00:05:31,113
She's scared to death.

172
00:05:31,293 --> 00:05:33,476
And I dialed the number for her.

173
00:05:33,656 --> 00:05:34,664
But by then,

174
00:05:34,664 --> 00:05:36,175
the line was dead.

175
00:05:36,525 --> 00:05:39,456
And then, at about midnight,

176
00:05:39,456 --> 00:05:41,759
Angela grabbed my arm,

177
00:05:41,759 --> 00:05:43,224
and said, Mrs.

178
00:05:43,404 --> 00:05:45,866
Miller, I think something's wrong.

179
00:05:46,046 --> 00:05:47,639
Her water had broken,

180
00:05:47,639 --> 00:05:50,597
honey, right there on my kitchen floor.

181
00:05:50,777 --> 00:05:52,719
And the roads were closed,

182
00:05:52,719 --> 00:05:55,109
and the phone lines were down by

183
00:05:55,109 --> 00:05:57,573
then, and there was nobody in the

184
00:05:57,573 --> 00:05:58,544
world but me.

185
00:05:58,724 --> 00:06:01,092
I'd had two babies of my own.

186
00:06:01,272 --> 00:06:02,440
But I had never,

187
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:03,827
ever delivered one.

188
00:06:04,177 --> 00:06:06,456
So I did what women have done

189
00:06:06,456 --> 00:06:08,263
for ten thousand years.

190
00:06:08,443 --> 00:06:09,578
I boiled water,

191
00:06:09,578 --> 00:06:12,150
because that's what they do in the

192
00:06:12,150 --> 00:06:15,100
movies, though I never figured out what

193
00:06:15,100 --> 00:06:15,932
it was for.

194
00:06:16,112 --> 00:06:18,511
I got every clean towel in the

195
00:06:18,511 --> 00:06:18,991
house.

196
00:06:19,171 --> 00:06:20,924
I made a bed of blankets in

197
00:06:20,924 --> 00:06:23,003
front of the stove in the living

198
00:06:23,003 --> 00:06:23,327
room.

199
00:06:23,507 --> 00:06:25,738
And I held Angela's hand,

200
00:06:25,738 --> 00:06:28,146
and I told her about my own

201
00:06:28,146 --> 00:06:30,912
two babies, every minute of it,

202
00:06:30,912 --> 00:06:32,161
over and over,

203
00:06:32,161 --> 00:06:33,678
to keep her calm.

204
00:06:34,028 --> 00:06:36,510
At two in the morning on Christmas

205
00:06:36,510 --> 00:06:38,482
Day, nineteen eighty-three,

206
00:06:38,482 --> 00:06:40,381
a baby girl was born on my

207
00:06:40,381 --> 00:06:41,695
living room floor,

208
00:06:41,695 --> 00:06:43,302
in front of the stove,

209
00:06:43,302 --> 00:06:45,858
by the light of the Christmas tree.

210
00:06:46,038 --> 00:06:48,267
Seven pounds, I'd guess.

211
00:06:48,447 --> 00:06:50,746
Loud and pink and perfect.

212
00:06:50,926 --> 00:06:53,682
I wrapped her in my mother's Christmas

213
00:06:53,682 --> 00:06:56,945
tablecloth, because it was the cleanest thing

214
00:06:56,945 --> 00:06:58,685
I had, and I laid her on

215
00:06:58,685 --> 00:06:59,773
Angela's chest.

216
00:06:59,953 --> 00:07:01,648
And we both cried.

217
00:07:01,998 --> 00:07:04,059
So far, the blizzard,

218
00:07:04,059 --> 00:07:05,434
the back door,

219
00:07:05,434 --> 00:07:07,594
the man, and the baby.

220
00:07:07,774 --> 00:07:09,495
At eight in the morning,

221
00:07:09,495 --> 00:07:11,360
the snowplow came through,

222
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:13,799
and the ambulance right behind it.

223
00:07:13,979 --> 00:07:16,759
The paramedics checked them both and said

224
00:07:16,759 --> 00:07:17,776
they were fine.

225
00:07:17,956 --> 00:07:20,113
One of them looked at me and

226
00:07:20,113 --> 00:07:23,041
said, ma'am, you did everything right.

227
00:07:23,221 --> 00:07:25,044
Where'd you learn that?

228
00:07:25,224 --> 00:07:26,349
And I said,

229
00:07:26,349 --> 00:07:27,987
honey, I didn't.

230
00:07:28,167 --> 00:07:30,140
I just didn't have a choice.

231
00:07:30,491 --> 00:07:33,312
Before they put her in the ambulance,

232
00:07:33,312 --> 00:07:35,599
Angela asked me my first name.

233
00:07:35,779 --> 00:07:37,602
I said, Ruth.

234
00:07:37,782 --> 00:07:38,794
And she said,

235
00:07:38,794 --> 00:07:40,429
then that's her name.

236
00:07:40,609 --> 00:07:43,371
Ruth Noelle, because she was born on

237
00:07:43,371 --> 00:07:44,138
Christmas.

238
00:07:44,318 --> 00:07:45,967
And then they were gone.

239
00:07:46,147 --> 00:07:47,953
Harold came home at noon,

240
00:07:47,953 --> 00:07:49,831
and I told him everything,

241
00:07:49,831 --> 00:07:51,998
and he sat down at the kitchen

242
00:07:51,998 --> 00:07:54,527
table and didn't say anything for a

243
00:07:54,527 --> 00:07:55,249
long time.

244
00:07:55,429 --> 00:07:56,586
Then he said,

245
00:07:56,586 --> 00:07:59,435
Ruthie, the rifle wasn't loaded.

246
00:07:59,615 --> 00:08:01,495
I said, I know.

247
00:08:01,846 --> 00:08:04,630
The man was arrested two days later,

248
00:08:04,630 --> 00:08:06,873
honey, in a bar in Mansfield.

249
00:08:07,053 --> 00:08:09,305
He'd been in trouble before.

250
00:08:09,485 --> 00:08:11,784
He went to prison for four years.

251
00:08:11,964 --> 00:08:14,841
Angela's mother came up from Kentucky and

252
00:08:14,841 --> 00:08:16,736
took her and the baby home.

253
00:08:16,916 --> 00:08:19,757
Angela sent me one letter that spring,

254
00:08:19,757 --> 00:08:22,523
with a picture of little Ruth Noelle.

255
00:08:22,703 --> 00:08:24,579
And then life went on,

256
00:08:24,579 --> 00:08:27,394
and I didn't hear from her again.

257
00:08:27,574 --> 00:08:29,036
For twenty years.

258
00:08:29,387 --> 00:08:31,785
And every Christmas Eve after that,

259
00:08:31,785 --> 00:08:34,253
honey, I'd think about that girl and

260
00:08:34,253 --> 00:08:35,760
that baby, and wonder.

261
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:37,763
Did she get away from him for

262
00:08:37,763 --> 00:08:38,077
good?

263
00:08:38,257 --> 00:08:39,940
Was the baby healthy?

264
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:41,988
Did she grow up knowing she was

265
00:08:41,988 --> 00:08:42,349
loved?

266
00:08:42,529 --> 00:08:44,608
I said a prayer for little Ruth

267
00:08:44,608 --> 00:08:47,692
Noelle every Christmas morning at two o'clock,

268
00:08:47,692 --> 00:08:49,837
because I'd wake up at that hour

269
00:08:49,837 --> 00:08:51,648
every year, like clockwork,

270
00:08:51,648 --> 00:08:53,257
for the rest of my life.

271
00:08:53,607 --> 00:08:56,293
Harold's brother told me once that I'd

272
00:08:56,293 --> 00:08:58,413
been a fool to open that door.

273
00:08:58,593 --> 00:08:59,802
He said, Ruth,

274
00:08:59,802 --> 00:09:02,738
that man could've killed you both.

275
00:09:02,918 --> 00:09:04,905
And maybe he was right,

276
00:09:04,905 --> 00:09:05,855
sweetheart.

277
00:09:06,035 --> 00:09:08,377
But I've thought about it for forty

278
00:09:08,377 --> 00:09:10,853
years, and I'd open it again tonight.

279
00:09:11,033 --> 00:09:14,075
Some doors you open because you're brave.

280
00:09:14,255 --> 00:09:16,629
Some you open because you know you

281
00:09:16,629 --> 00:09:19,561
couldn't live with yourself if you didn't.

282
00:09:19,911 --> 00:09:21,287
On Christmas Eve,

283
00:09:21,287 --> 00:09:22,825
two thousand three,

284
00:09:22,825 --> 00:09:25,416
Harold and I were sitting by the

285
00:09:25,416 --> 00:09:27,116
fire, two old people,

286
00:09:27,116 --> 00:09:28,978
when the doorbell rang.

287
00:09:29,158 --> 00:09:30,991
It was snowing again,

288
00:09:30,991 --> 00:09:32,736
not like that night,

289
00:09:32,736 --> 00:09:34,394
just a gentle snow.

290
00:09:34,574 --> 00:09:36,623
And on my porch stood a woman

291
00:09:36,623 --> 00:09:39,307
about forty, with a young woman beside

292
00:09:39,307 --> 00:09:39,590
her.

293
00:09:39,770 --> 00:09:42,657
Tall, dark-haired, in a nurse's coat,

294
00:09:42,657 --> 00:09:45,155
with a little name tag pinned to

295
00:09:45,155 --> 00:09:45,389
it.

296
00:09:45,569 --> 00:09:47,617
The name tag said,

297
00:09:47,617 --> 00:09:48,413
Ruth N.

298
00:09:48,593 --> 00:09:49,905
Carter, R.

299
00:09:50,085 --> 00:09:51,118
N.

300
00:09:51,469 --> 00:09:53,674
Angela said, Mrs.

301
00:09:53,854 --> 00:09:56,827
Miller, do you remember me?

302
00:09:57,007 --> 00:09:59,264
And I didn't even answer,

303
00:09:59,264 --> 00:10:00,257
sweetheart.

304
00:10:00,437 --> 00:10:03,003
I just pulled them both inside and

305
00:10:03,003 --> 00:10:03,758
held them.

306
00:10:03,938 --> 00:10:06,446
Ruth Noelle was twenty years old,

307
00:10:06,446 --> 00:10:07,966
and she was a nurse,

308
00:10:07,966 --> 00:10:10,474
in the labor and delivery ward at

309
00:10:10,474 --> 00:10:12,298
a hospital in Lexington,

310
00:10:12,298 --> 00:10:12,982
Kentucky.

311
00:10:13,162 --> 00:10:15,879
She said, Mama told me the story

312
00:10:15,879 --> 00:10:17,237
every Christmas.

313
00:10:17,417 --> 00:10:19,863
About the lady who delivered me on

314
00:10:19,863 --> 00:10:21,446
her living room floor.

315
00:10:21,626 --> 00:10:23,367
I wanted to do the same.

316
00:10:23,718 --> 00:10:26,365
And then she handed me a box.

317
00:10:26,545 --> 00:10:28,367
Inside, folded neatly,

318
00:10:28,367 --> 00:10:31,432
was my mother's Christmas tablecloth.

319
00:10:31,612 --> 00:10:33,528
The one I'd wrapped her in.

320
00:10:33,708 --> 00:10:36,649
Angela had kept it for twenty years,

321
00:10:36,649 --> 00:10:38,201
washed and pressed.

322
00:10:38,381 --> 00:10:40,056
And on top of it was a

323
00:10:40,056 --> 00:10:42,491
little book, a nurse's notebook.

324
00:10:42,671 --> 00:10:44,570
Ruth Noelle said,

325
00:10:44,570 --> 00:10:45,016
Mrs.

326
00:10:45,196 --> 00:10:48,807
Miller, I've delivered sixty-three babies this year.

327
00:10:48,987 --> 00:10:51,170
I write every one of their names

328
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:51,715
in here.

329
00:10:51,895 --> 00:10:53,138
Because of you.

330
00:10:53,488 --> 00:10:55,656
Angela told me the rest at my

331
00:10:55,656 --> 00:10:56,704
kitchen table.

332
00:10:56,884 --> 00:10:58,193
She'd gone home,

333
00:10:58,193 --> 00:10:59,911
finished high school,

334
00:10:59,911 --> 00:11:02,120
and become a social worker.

335
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:05,272
She'd spent fifteen years running a shelter

336
00:11:05,272 --> 00:11:06,793
for women in Kentucky.

337
00:11:06,973 --> 00:11:08,552
Women like she'd been,

338
00:11:08,552 --> 00:11:11,425
running through the snow with nowhere to

339
00:11:11,425 --> 00:11:11,640
go.

340
00:11:11,820 --> 00:11:13,736
She said, Mrs.

341
00:11:13,916 --> 00:11:16,656
Miller, there's a sign over our door.

342
00:11:16,836 --> 00:11:19,448
It says, the light is always on.

343
00:11:19,628 --> 00:11:20,696
That's from you.

344
00:11:21,046 --> 00:11:23,933
They've come every Christmas Eve since,

345
00:11:23,933 --> 00:11:24,378
honey.

346
00:11:24,558 --> 00:11:27,345
Ruth Noelle has three children of her

347
00:11:27,345 --> 00:11:29,831
own now, and she's the head nurse

348
00:11:29,831 --> 00:11:31,187
of her whole ward.

349
00:11:31,367 --> 00:11:33,068
And every Christmas Eve,

350
00:11:33,068 --> 00:11:35,266
I leave my kitchen light on all

351
00:11:35,266 --> 00:11:36,046
night long.

352
00:11:36,226 --> 00:11:38,671
Harold used to tease me about the

353
00:11:38,671 --> 00:11:39,709
electric bill.

354
00:11:39,889 --> 00:11:40,811
I'd tell him,

355
00:11:40,811 --> 00:11:42,443
somebody might need it.

356
00:11:42,623 --> 00:11:44,765
You never know who's out there in

357
00:11:44,765 --> 00:11:47,036
the dark, looking for the one light

358
00:11:47,036 --> 00:11:47,685
that's on.

359
00:11:48,035 --> 00:11:50,057
Tell me in the comments,

360
00:11:50,057 --> 00:11:50,983
sweetheart.

361
00:11:51,163 --> 00:11:53,764
Would you have opened that back door?

362
00:11:53,944 --> 00:11:55,976
Be honest with Grandma.

363
00:11:56,156 --> 00:11:58,683
And if anyone ever opened their door

364
00:11:58,683 --> 00:12:00,578
for you when you needed it,

365
00:12:00,578 --> 00:12:02,263
I want to hear about it.

366
00:12:02,443 --> 00:12:04,825
There are more of my family's stories

367
00:12:04,825 --> 00:12:07,078
in the playlist right there on your

368
00:12:07,078 --> 00:12:09,073
screen, and I'll see you in the

369
00:12:09,073 --> 00:12:09,653
next one.

370
00:12:09,833 --> 00:12:11,307
Good night, honey.

371
00:12:11,487 --> 00:12:12,985
Leave your light on.
